Role Purpose
Evaluate the efficacy of business processes, internal controls and risk management procedures currently in place and make recommendations on how to improve internal controls and governance processes. The position holder will use various tools to diagnose and highlight inefficiencies in the SOPs, policies and day to day transactions of the company.
He/she will conduct and direct audits and ongoing reviews of organization controls, operating procedures and oversee compliance with policies and regulations to review and appraise the soundness, effectiveness and proper application of all internal controls and compliance procedures.
Key Responsibilities:
Internal controls framework: Lead the development and implementation of the internal controls & risk management framework and policy. Continuously review and monitor existing systems to improve their effectiveness and increase the organization’s process maturity levels. Develop operational capabilities to ensure the company can survive adverse effects; lead diagnosis and highlight inefficiencies, fraud and revenue leakage.
Risk Management:Test the controls set by the organization’s management (for vulnerabilities) and give recommendations on how to mitigate against risks. Participate in end-user testing of applications, systems and dashboards pointing out any inconsistencies or variations from the business requirements. Develop key risk indicators for the business; advise management on enterprise risk; continually identify new and emerging risks facing the company and maintain an up-to-date risk profile. Quantify the probability & severity of the current and emerging risks.
Operational Efficiency:Conduct regular reviews of the internal controls system to ensure that necessary modifications and improvements are identified and made on time. In partnership with Line Managers develop appropriate robust mitigation actions on gaps identified. Align the ERP to business processes by advising the technology department from a control and process optimization standpoint.
Internal Audit: Evaluate the application of internal operational guidelines/manuals, identify deviations and recommend appropriate changes whenever necessary. Develop and maintain the internal audit procedures to ensure that best practice is taken into account and that the audits address specific areas of Internal controls & risk management.
Compliance:Ensure that Line Managers and key staff in control functions are well aware of the company's Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) and processes and drive adherence to the SOPs.
Reporting:Compile and discuss reports detailing findings, implications and recommendations for system improvements. Prepare comprehensive regular and special reports to the leadership team in the business, highlighting identified gaps. Deliver relevant material information to all relevant stakeholders. Expand data sources & collection to populate control and process optimization reports.
Training:Oversee the organization of regular training and awareness for the staff on the Internal control process to develop an understanding of the same. Document and report material changes affecting the company’s internal control system to help ensure that the framework is reviewed, maintained and improved appropriately.
Minimum Qualifications & Desired Skills
A bachelor’s degree in Business or related field;
An MBA is an added advantage;
At least 5 - 6 years in internal controls and risk management;
Knowledge and appreciation of internal controls, finance or risk management;
Adept in process management;
Proven understanding and application of internal controls management frameworks;
Proficiency is any statistical software will be an added advantage;
Critical understanding in the establishment and operation of internal control mechanisms;
Proven track record of working with cross-functional teams;
Ability to make presentations and lead workshops with ease;
Ability to articulate complex ideas in an understandable manner.
Competencies & Skills:
Strong Financial Acumen;
Strategic Orientation;
Business Acumen;
Detail Orientation;
Analytical Thinking;
Stakeholder Management;
Investigative mindset;
Output oriented;
Tech Savvy.

Job Summary
We seek an individual with a strong Global Business Knowledge, and an experience in Strategy Formulation and Execution, Business Performance Management, Change Management, and an ability to apply conceptual thinking in driving strategic decision amongst other areas listed:
Responsibilities
Articulate the Group’s mission in clear and concise terms that can speak to stakeholders across the Group;
Develop an inclusive strategy and strategic plans by collaborating with Leadership across the Group.
Collaborate with the subsidiary CEOs and other business leaders, special committees and consultants to execute strategies;
Create actionable goals across Group that make it possible to turn our mission into tangible results;
Engage in ongoing analyses of market dynamics, market share changes, product line performance and competitive intelligence to protect market position or create new markets;
Identify key capital projects, joint ventures, and other strategic partnership opportunities in line with agreed go-to market strategies and growth plans;
Ensure suitable metrics are in place to measure performance and progress across the Group;
Collaborate with Executive Management across the Group and its subsidiaries to devise effective short- and long-term plans and develop KPIs in line with business objectives;
Align project prioritisation with Group goals;
Lead the organisation’s approach to measurement and evaluation with a focus on creating effective organisational dashboards for achieving impact;
Coordinate all Project Management activities across the Group;
Engage external business and industry experts to learn and influence business strategies, constantly remaining alert and forward-thinking about opportunities and risks in the industry;
Develop and implement a comprehensive competitive strategy document for the Group;
Person Specification & Required Qualification (s)
B.Sc./HND degree from a reputable institution;
An MBA or any other relevant degree is an added advantage;
Professional qualifications/certifications; CFA, ACA, FCA, CIS, CIBN, is an added advantage;
A minimum of ten (10) years’ cognate experience is required, with at least 5 years’ experience in a Senior Management role in a Group/Holding structure;
A visionary with a deep knowledge of what is required to lead the Strategy Function in a Group/Holding Company (HoldCo);
Ability to build strong partnerships with small, medium and large businesses and communicate effectively to a wide variety of audiences;
Must possess strong working knowledge of management strategies, project management, human resource planning, business performance management, technology, and the core businesses of the respective subsidiaries;
Must be able to multitask with research, projects, analysis as well as interpret data effectively for decision making;
An articulate, confident, and excellent communicator.

Job Purpose
The Employer, Elim Christian Vocational Training Centre, an NGO located in Benue State is in need to hire for a definite period, a Project Finance Officer to support Elim CVTC’s projects – Community Based Inclusive Development in Benue State. The Project Finance Officer is accountable and responsible for day-to-day financial management of the project including but not limited to reviewing, disbursing cash or giving cash advances, confirming staff retirement, documenting/filing, preparing finance reports, preparing audit. He/she should be accountable to Elim management (Finance manager and Director) and any other duty that may be assigned by Elim Finance Manager or Directors. On no occasion shall the employee share any information concerning the project however small or big with third party or anybody without prior permission/approval from Elim Finance Manager or Director.
He/she will therefore ensure efficient and effective monitoring, supervision and documentation of all financial transactions of the project.
He/she will report to Elim CVTC Finance Manager or Director (that notwithstanding, he can also relate with and seek for support of donors’ Project Focal Person(s) after obtaining permission or approval for such from Elim Finance Manager or Director).
The Finance Officer will ensure that the project team complies with Elim CVTC and donors’ Policies and Procedure and the Principle of stewardship. This person will provide oversight in funds management and accounting (processing of financial data according to donor requirements, verifying accuracy of data, implementing accounting policies and procedures, generating prompt and accurate financial reports) within the Elim CVTC project, support the project team in keeping with internal control systems and providing feedback on budget performance within the project.
The Finance Officer will be directly responsible for all financial and administrative tasks and procedures as well as the logistics functions for the project, and ensure that internal control systems are kept in line with project financial regulations and international standards. He/she will work closely with the Project Coordinators, Programme Manager and donors’ representatives to drive best practices in financial management and administration, while supporting Elim CVTC in improvement of accounting systems.
Roles and responsibilities
Ensure that complete and accurate accounting records for all projects’ transactions are maintained, and reviewed in a timely manner;
Responsible for entering financial information and maintaining all financial records for projects and for the organization;
Ensure proper documentation of all payment requests and vouchers, proper filing and completeness of supporting documents;
Manage financial control, prepare and analyze budgets, develop financial reports, and make recommendations to the organization on budget expenditures
Responsible for the preparation of balance sheets, income statement, expense reports and other financial records
Assist and/or lead budget development, account balance management, tax remittance, tax return compilation and activity budget reviews
Prepare monthly bank reconciliations and petty cash management;
Responsible for weekly/monthly/quarterly/bi-annual/annual finance update and reports and report same to Elim Finance Manager and donors;
Ensure that all financial reporting is completed on time and submitted to donors;
Monitor the expenditures to ensure that program funds are utilized appropriately by the close of the fiscal year;
Preparing monthly management accounts, including cashflow forecasts, and other reports;
Assist with audit preparation, auditor reviews and implementation of recommendations as directed;
Develop financial policies to ensure operational efficiency;
Other tasks as required by Elim CVTC.
Qualification
Bachelor’s degree in accounting
At least two years’ experience in accounting or other finance related field
Previous experience in the NGO or development sector – is desirable
Strong intellectual ability and professional financial experience, as evidenced by a formal qualification or part qualification in accountancy (AAT, ICAN, ACCA, etc.) or experience of working as a finance officer or a similar role will be an advantage.
Ready to abide by rules/regulations guiding Elim/donors
Required Skills
Excellent IT skills, with specific competency in Microsoft Excel. Previous experience using accounting software (
QuickBooks
) highly desirable.
Should be well vested with the ability to carry out e-banking (online banking) transactions
Ability to work in a team environment with technical and non-technical staff.
Strong verbal and written communication skills
Self-motivated and dynamic, with excellent organizational skills and a keen attention to detail.
Reliable, honest and trustworthy.
Behaviours (Values in practice)
Accountability:
Holds self-accountable for making decisions, managing resources efficiently, achieving results together with vulnerable groups, especially children and adults-at-risk, and role modelling Elim CVTC values;
Ambition:
Sets ambitious and challenging goals for self and team, takes responsibility for own personal development and encourages team to do the same;
Widely shares personal vision for Elim CVTC, engages and motivates others;
Future oriented, thinks strategically and on a global scale.
Collaboration:
Builds and maintains effective relationships, with own team, project team, Elim CVTC staff and field workers, and partner staff;
Values diversity, sees it as a source of competitive strength;
Approachable, good listener, easy to talk to.
Creativity:
Develops and encourages new and innovative solutions;
Willing to take disciplined risks.
Integrity:
Honest, encourages openness and transparency;
Always acts in the best interests of children and adults-at-risk.

Key responsibilities:
Participate with M&E team in supervision of data collection for nutrition and health assessments;
Liaise with Nutrition Assistants for accessing community support group and health facility database on a regular basis and updating overall health facility based activities;
Conduct ongoing capacity assessment of health workers on CMAM services delivery, IMCI service delivery, reproductive health service delivery, vaccination etc. and review the training needs and/or coaching needs;
